  "content": {
    "id": "p15-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Solve the simultaneous equations\n$$\\begin{aligned}x&=16y,\\\\\\log_y x-\\log_x y&=\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(x,y)=(2,\\frac18)$ or $(64,4)$.\n\nLet $m=\\log_y x$ and solve $m-\\frac1m=\\frac83$.",
      "worked": "The logarithms require $x,y>0$ and $x,y\\ne1$. Let $m=\\log_y x$. By change of base, $\\log_x y=\\frac1m$.\n$$\\begin{align*}m-\\frac1m&=\\frac83\\\\3m^2-3&=8m\\\\3m^2-8m-3&=0\\\\(3m+1)(m-3)&=0\\\\m&=-\\frac13\\text{ or }3.\\end{align*}$$\nFor $m=-\\frac13$, substitute $x=16y$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_y(16y)&=-\\frac13\\\\\\log_y16+1&=-\\frac13\\\\\\log_y16&=-\\frac43\\\\y^{-4/3}&=16\\\\y&=16^{-3/4}=\\frac18\\\\x&=16\\left(\\frac18\\right)=2.\\end{align*}$$\nFor $m=3$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_y(16y)&=3\\\\\\log_y16+1&=3\\\\\\log_y16&=2\\\\y^2&=16\\\\y&=4\\\\x&=16(4)=64.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth pairs satisfy the domain restrictions. Checking the original logarithmic equation:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{1/8}2-\\log_2(1/8)&=-\\frac13-(-3)=\\frac83\\\\\\log_4 64-\\log_{64}4&=3-\\frac13=\\frac83.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, $(x,y)=(2,\\frac18)$ or $(64,4)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 118
  },
